; GLQuakeStack -- GLQuake started with a small stack (Stack 100000), as a
; user may from the shell. The A4000D crashed with a guru that way
; (2026-11-02): GLQuake needs 768 KB and the GCC build never asked for it.
; GLQuake now grows its own stack (glquake/sys_amiga.c, QUAKE_STACK): demo1
; must run to its end on the null card and the program must exit cleanly,
; its stack freed (Avail before and after).
; Needs: gmake glquake glquake-data rgl-lib.
; LIMIT 900
FailAt 1000
Wait 12
Echo "=== machine ===" >DEV:Test/auto.log
CPU >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/null-#?
Avail >NIL: FLUSH
Echo "=== free before ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Avail FLUSH >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Stack 100000
Echo "=== demo1 with Stack 100000 ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/RunNull demo1
Execute DEV:Test/WaitDone DEV:Test/null-demo1.done
Type DEV:Test/null-demo1.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Type DEV:Test/null-demo1-lib.log >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== free after ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Avail FLUSH >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo "=== done ===" >>DEV:Test/auto.log
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
